($f$080b7013-14b2-4fd8-be8b-f567db3cdb39$f$, 17700929, $f$call the night by name$f$, ARRAY[$f$erlkoenig$f$]::text[], ARRAY[$f$The Silmarillion and other histories of Middle-Earth - J. R. R. Tolkien$f$, $f$TOLKIEN J. R. R. - Works & Related Fandoms$f$]::text[], NULL, ARRAY[]::text[], $f$They were surrounded, the orcs pressing their advantage into the fen. The ground slick and soft beneath them, beneath even elven feet, giving way and allowing the enemy to gain ground. And himself, his men still so far away, bodies falling around him, friend and foe alike as he thought, let me closer, if I can just get to them.$f$, 6133, 1, 1, true, 3, false, $f$2019-07-29T11:17:56.206+00:00$f$, $f$2019-07-29T11:17:56.274+00:00$f$, $f$2019-02-08T00:00:00.000+00:00$f$, false, false, true, NULL, NULL, ARRAY[]::text[]),
($f$080b7013-14b2-4fd8-be8b-f567db3cdb39$f$, 17715437, $f$Ever At His Side$f$, ARRAY[$f$Anonymous$f$]::text[], ARRAY[$f$Original Work$f$]::text[], NULL, ARRAY[]::text[], $f$Sir Asoza has for more than two decades been a good friend and trusted knight to the ruler of Athelney; he has been in love with him almost as long. When it seems like the pressure at court is getting to King Lyndon, Sir Asoza proposes a small stay at his own keep to get away from politics for a bit. In their shared solitude, however, their feelings suddenly become hard to ignore.$f$, 10917, 1, 1, true, 1, false, $f$2019-02-16T12:54:30.525+00:00$f$, $f$2019-02-16T12:54:30.619+00:00$f$, $f$2019-02-15T00:00:00.000+00:00$f$, false, false, true, NULL, NULL, ARRAY[]::text[]),
